# .gitattributes — repo-weight hygiene (WIN #15)
#
# Purpose:
#   1) Normalize text line endings so the repo stores LF and avoids
#      noisy CRLF/LF churn across Windows + CI + worktrees.
#   2) Mark known binary/asset types as binary so Git never tries to
#      diff/merge them (and never corrupts them with EOL conversion).
#
# This file is a config-only hygiene change. It does NOT move anything
# into Git LFS and does NOT rewrite history. For the LFS migration plan
# see: docs/GIT_LFS_PLAN.md
#
# NOTE: `binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff -merge`. Files marked
# binary are never EOL-normalized, never diffed, never auto-merged.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: let Git decide text vs binary and normalize text to LF on
# commit. Working-tree checkout EOL is left to each user's core.autocrlf
# / core.eol, except where pinned explicitly below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pin line endings for code that MUST stay LF (shell, Python, JS family).
# Prevents shebang/CRLF breakage and keeps engine sources byte-stable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.pyi   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary / asset types — no diff, no merge, no EOL conversion.
# (Required set per WIN #15.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.tga   binary
*.psd   binary
*.zip   binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.pyd   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pak   binary
*.dat   binary
*.mat   binary
*.npz   binary
